{
  "revised_script": {
    "cold_open": "The library was quiet, save for the soft rustle of pages. A book with no title sat on the desk, waiting.",
    "question": "Who returns this book every ten years, unchanged by time?",
    "journey": "The librarian watched as a woman returned the book, just as she had a decade before. The woman's face was the same, her smile familiar. Each time, she came alone, placed the book gently on the desk, and left without a word. The librarian wondered who she was and why she returned the book, but never asked. The years passed, and the woman returned, always on the same day, always unchanged.",
    "discovery": "One day, the librarian found a note tucked inside the book. It read: 'I return this book to keep the story alive. Each time, I begin again.' The book was filled with the same story, written in the same hand, yet each version had subtle differences.",
    "emotional_turn": "The librarian realized the woman was not just returning a book—she was returning herself, preserving a memory that could not fade.",
    "payoff": "The woman had returned the book to honor a lost love, a story that lived on through the pages. The librarian understood, and from that day on, the book was never alone again.",
    "after_image": "The library remained quiet, but now it held a secret."
  },
